{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defects found. The targeted tests and strict artifact/surface checks passed. Both broad local validation runs failed, including a 600-second unit-test timeout; approval relies on the supplied sealed validation evidence, not those reruns. The worktree remains unchanged.\n\nRules applied: pose-review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence. Knowledge governance was consulted; no knowledge artifacts were changed.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared R1-R3 with the diff and existing apply path. Verified that catalog adoption mutates freshly loaded in-memory policy maps. The spec explicitly acknowledges that adopt.values lacks a direct assertion; its behavior was inspected in code. Broad local validation failed, so full-suite assurance rests on the supplied sealed evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The added preview performs synchronous reads and local map mutations; it adds no goroutines, lifecycle ownership or publication changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds the specified preview fields while preserving request arguments, pair-flag refusal and apply behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing request validation remains intact. Policy-load failures return contextual errors and stop processing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed the configuration-review request, adoption CLI and setup composition. Targeted tests passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The preview now exposes catalog changes through adopt.change and provides actionable closeout-value guidance without adding sensitive output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected CLI parsing and application. Existing arguments, persisted policy formats and MCP contracts remain unchanged; additional human-readable preview fields are declared by the spec.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The preview invokes the same catalog adoption function as apply, using the selected date. The focused regression, configuration-review and pair-refusal tests passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1's cause was omission of catalog mutations from the request preview. Reusing entry.Adopt on freshly loaded maps exposes those mutations without changing persistence. The closeout-specific message addresses R2, and the four attribution edits address R3. No individual structural delta facts were listed in the supplied brief.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected all four manual diffs. English and Portuguese source and scaffold copies consistently attribute the sandboxed profile to pose-dist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected adopt.go: policy changes are printed before adopt.apply, and the closeout guidance names both value flags and their accepted alternatives.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is covered by the focused regression and apply-path comparison. R2 was verified against the closeout catalog defaults and emitted guidance; its direct-test gap is disclosed in the spec. R3 was verified across all four manual changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the requested range with the spec's artifacts and non-goals. The change is limited to preview reporting, its regression/check registration, manual attribution and governance records. It does not change what an answer applies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the added reads, catalog lookup, output and existing answer validation. The change adds no command execution, caller-controlled path, credential handling or authority bypass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing the existing catalog mutator is a small sufficient fix and avoids duplicating policy-key descriptions. The capability-specific guidance is bounded to the present requirement. This choice would need reconsideration if catalog adoption gained external side effects or stopped being safe on isolated in-memory maps.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --strict --from 43099880d96a55d195811bf1f5269a9a3d14073d --to 5c3c804541a1e5020bb41be2b284c61fe65227af --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran verification bound to the requested range; exit 0, with no error or critical findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the supplied sealed structure evidence and independently inspected the spec, diff and catalog/apply relationship. Did not regenerate assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A component-wide assessment refresh was unnecessary for this bounded review and could write repository assessment state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the existing CLI/domain boundary and supplied integration evidence. No REST, event, Protobuf or MCP contract changed; did not regenerate assessment sta